{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract info [-h] [--detailed] [--format {tsv,parquet}] [--cache | --no-cache] [--csv]\n                       <command> ...\n\npositional arguments:\n  <command>\n    calculate-coverage  Generate a full breadth-of-coverage report. Uses samtools coverage to\n                        calculate exactly how much of each chromosome was sequenced.\n    coverage-sample     Quickly estimate per-chromosome breadth of coverage by sampling ~1,000\n                        evenly spaced, length-weighted 1 kb windows. An estimate; use calculate-\n                        coverage for exact numbers.\n    gene                Look at one gene from local data: its span and RefSeq transcripts, your\n                        VCF's variants in it with consequence, ClinVar, gnomAD and research-only\n                        ACMG annotations, and BAM/CRAM read depth over each exon against a\n                        callable threshold. Nothing is downloaded; missing data names the command\n                        that makes it.\n    chip                Identify the vendor, chip and revision of a consumer microarray raw-data\n                        file (23andMe, AncestryDNA, MyHeritage, FTDNA, ...) from its header and\n                        marker set, with a confidence score and the matching --formats template.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --detailed            Perform full index and body sample analysis (detailed mode)\n  --format {tsv,parquet}\n                        Also save the per-chromosome table and the QC stats as <input>_chromosomes\n                        and <input>_qc .tsv or .parquet (needs pyarrow); implies --detailed\n  --cache, --no-cache   Save the metrics as <input>.wgse_info.json for later runs (default: on)\n  --csv                 Output the table as CSV instead of formatted text\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract info --input sample.cram\n  wgsextract info --input sample.cram --detailed\n  wgsextract info --input sample.cram --format parquet\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  Prints a summary and caches it as <input file name>.wgse_info.json; with\n  --format also <input file name>_chromosomes and _qc (QC stats) as .tsv or\n  .parquet.\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools; seconds on a 30x\n  genome.\n",
